  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-TZA151</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened labour administrative services through workplace compliance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO supports the United Republic of Tanzania in enhancing labour administrative systems to promote workplace compliance and improve labour protections. This CPO focuses on strengthening social dialogue and labour relations institutions, empowering tripartite constituents to contribute effectively to economic and social policies, and addressing labour disputes through improved mediation and arbitration mechanisms.

Key interventions include capacity-building for the Labour, Economic and Social Council (LESCO) and the Zanzibar Labour Advisory Board (LAB) to enable effective social dialogue, as well as enhancing the performance of the Commission for Mediation and Arbitration (CMA) and the Dispute Handling Unit (DHU). These efforts aim to ensure effective dispute resolution, compliance with labour laws, and access to justice for workers and employers.

The programme also prioritizes empowering labour inspectorates through strategic compliance planning, development of tools such as labour inspection manuals, and introducing modern systems for data management and case tracking. Special attention is given to vulnerable groups, including domestic workers, to extend labour protections and ensure access to justice.

These efforts contribute to SDG 8 (Decent Work and Economic Growth), SDG 16 (Peace, Justice, and Strong Institutions), and SDG 3 (Good Health and Well-being) by fostering inclusive labour practices and building the capacity of key stakeholders. The initiative aligns with the Decent Work Country Programme (DWCP) and complements ongoing UN efforts to strengthen labour market governance in Tanzania.</narrative>
  </description>
